# A committing forage brain: the reactive floor plus a saturating commitment
# channel. `mem` slowly integrates motor activity (clamped so the positive
# feedback cannot run away) and feeds it back, so whichever target currently
# leads gets amplified and KEPT — hysteresis at the decision. This is the cure
# for the observed reactive limit cycle: standing between two foods whose pulls
# flip winner every step until the player starves. First brain to reliably eat
# more than once per life on the wide maze.

channel food
channel wall
channel mem: init 0
channel motor: init 0
channel avoid: init 0

rule commit:
  when 1
  set mem = clamp(0.99 * mem + 0.02 * motor, 0, 2)

rule go:
  when 1
  set motor = 0.4 * avg8(motor) + food + 0.5 * mem

rule fear:
  when 1
  set avoid = 0.4 * avg8(avoid) + 0.5 * wall
